# Veripsa release gate (auto-discovered). One gate per file -> two PRs adding gates add two FILES, never a
# shared line -> no false merge conflict on registration. register_gate is defined in run_gates.sh.
# Format: register_gate <test> <marker> <name> <ok_blurb> <desc> [tail]
# GATE-HYGIENE: description strings must contain NO dollar-sign and NO backtick (set -u in the runner).
register_gate "tests/test_cross_substrate_api.py" "API-CONTRACT SUBSTRATE GATE: PASS" "API-contract cross-substrate coupling: GraphQL type definitions + protobuf service/message definitions referenced from code" "api-contract substrate: GraphQL type definition couples to anchored references (resolver map + gql template, crown-jewel, no code edge); precision: Query/Mutation/String/ID do NOT mint api_type nodes; protobuf: service+message definition couples to client stub/message references (no code edge); precision: unanchored prose word equal to a GraphQL type name does NOT couple; never-crash: empty + binary-ish .graphql/.proto do not raise; content-free: a secret in a comment never appears in graph output; additive: pure-Python repo gets zero api_* nodes (no regression)." "API-contract cross-substrate: a GraphQL type defined in a .graphql schema and referenced from a resolver map or a gql/graphql tagged template, or a protobuf service/message defined in a .proto and referenced by hand-written gRPC client code, are coupled via a shared api_type/api_message/api_service node with NO import/call edge -- the crown-jewel coupling structural tools miss (the schema/proto is its own language and the generated bridge stubs are excluded as vendored). Two-pass known-set discipline (mirrors _cg_schema/_cg_iac): pass 1 collects locally-defined contract symbols; pass 2 emits a queries edge only for ANCHORED references to KNOWN names (gql/graphql tagged templates, .graphql/.gql operation files, resolver-map keys, exact or stub-suffixed proto identifiers). PRECISION guards: a stoplist drops ubiquitous names (GraphQL Query/Mutation/Subscription and built-in scalars String/Int/Float/Boolean/ID; generic proto words), and comments are stripped on the reference side so a type name appearing only in prose never fabricates a coupling. REUSES the existing alters (definer) / queries (referencer) edge kinds so the shared-resource adjacency couples the files with NO SQL change. Content-free (contract symbol names and file paths only, never field values, message bodies, schema field definitions, or comment content). Never-crash (file reads and scans are bounded and guarded). Gate 131." 9
